sentences.text:
In the interim, it is ordered that petitioners shall be released on bail, in the event of their arrest, in case FIR No.129, dated 12.09.2023, under Sections 498A, 406, 323, 504, 506, 469, 120B &
34 of the Indian Penal Code, registered at Police Station Nahan, District Sirmaur, H.P., on their furnishing personal bond to the tune of Rs.50,000/- each, with one surety each in the like amount to the satisfaction of the Investigating Officer, subject to the following conditions:-
1. That the petitioners will join investigation of case as and when called for by the Investigating Officer, in accordance with law;
2. That they will not directly or indirectly make any inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the facts of the case so as to dissuade him/her from disclosing such facts to the Investigating Officer or Court;
3. That they will not tamper with the prosecution evidence nor they will try to win over the prosecution witnesses in any manner;
4. That they will not leave India without prior permission of the Court.
.

